    {
      "id": "graph-application-template-catalog-item-88",
      "type": "topic-synthesis",
      "label": "Architecture & guardrails",
      "position": {
        "x": -2300,
        "y": 450
      },
      "width": 470,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Architecture & guardrails",
        "summary": "# Three distinct layers\n\n**Template:** Defines how a concept is represented in Twilite.\n\n**Converter:** Translates external serialization or API records into the Twilite model. Preserve identity, edges, ports, metadata and provenance.\n\n**Provider:** Connects to an external runtime for reading, writing or execution; permissions and auditability are enforced here.\n\n## First five families\nEntity · Workflow · Function · Resource · Schema.\n\n## First proof\nImport one real n8n workflow and inspect it; separately derive a Salesforce schema graph. Do not let converter work become a new core rewrite.\n\n## Cautions\nImport ≠ execution. Graph appearance ≠ faithful semantics. A visual edge ≠ authorization. Browser embeds may require desktop runtime.",
        "openQuestions": "Which conversions are lossless? Which require runtime adapters?",
        "definitionKey": "topic-synthesis",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "topic-synthesis",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-synthesis.node-class.node",
